 but E12 is X, so Black gets diagonal two.  \n\nSo D13 is a key point for both sides.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nD13 is a dual-purpose move: it blocks Black’s most dangerous open two (C13-E13) while building a vertical pair for White (D12-D13). It’s central in the cluster. Other moves like F9 or H10 are less urgent.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"col": "D", "row": 13}'}
