entral presence and creates potential for future threats (like creating a three with F10 and E11 horizontally? Actually F11 and E11 are horizontal neighbors? F11 and E11 are col F and E, row 11, so they are adjacent horizontally? Yes, they are adjacent horizontally: E11 and F11 are adjacent. So playing F11 creates a horizontal pair E11-F11, and also a vertical pair F10-F11. This move also indirectly supports the diagonal with G10 (since F11 and G10 are diagonal). It’s a flexible move that builds momentum and doesn’t leave an immediate open three for Black. It also blocks any Black horizontal at row 11.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "F", "row": 11}'}
